        "original_id": "39f5eec0-3790-5742-afb8-0fee523d91d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Eastern Air Defense Sector, North American Aerospace Defense Command, Continental U.S. NORAD Region, 1st Air Force, Air Combat Command, Advisory Committee on Antarctic Names, New York Air National Guard\n- Places: Tyndall Air Force Base, Panama City, Florida, Mount Knauff\n- People: Robert A. Knauff\n- Roles: chief of staff, adjutant general\n\nFacts:\n- The Eastern Air Defense Sector is a United States Air Force Air Combat Command unit permanently assigned to the North American Aerospace Defense Command.\n- The Eastern Air Defense Sector is a subordinate command of the Continental U.S. NORAD Region-1st Air Force, which is headquartered at Tyndall Air Force Base in Florida.\n- Tyndall Air Force Base is a United States Air Force base located 12 miles east of Panama City, Florida.\n- Mount Knauff was named by the Advisory Committee on Antarctic Names after Major General Robert A. Knauff.\n- Robert A. Knauff was chief of staff of the New York Air National Guard.\n- Robert A. Knauff supervised five flying wings and the Eastern Air Defense Sector.\n- Robert A. Knauff was the primary advisor to the adjutant general on Air Guard matters.",
